# 必考词 Unit29
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2023红宝书考研英语词汇-必考词
# 描述: 必考词Unit29核心高频词汇

{{glare}}{/ɡleər/}}{v. 怒视；n. 强光}}{{She glared at him angrily after the rude remark.}}

{{gleam}}{/ɡliːm/}}{v. 闪烁；n. 微光}}{{The polished floor gleamed in the sunlight.}}

{{glimpse}}{/ɡlɪmps/}}{n. 一瞥；v. 瞥见}}{{She caught a glimpse of the celebrity in the crowd.}}

{{gloomy}}{/ˈɡluːmi/}}{adj. 阴暗的；忧郁的}}{{The rainy weather made everyone feel gloomy.}}

{{gorgeous}}{/ˈɡɔːrdʒəs/}}{adj. 华丽的；极好的}}{{The view from the mountaintop was absolutely gorgeous.}}

{{gratitude}}{/ˈɡrætɪtjuːd/}}{n. 感激；感谢}}{{He expressed his gratitude to everyone who helped him.}}

{{grieve}}{/ɡriːv/}}{v. 悲伤；哀悼}}{{The whole nation grieved the loss of the great leader.}}

{{grip}}{/ɡrɪp/}}{v. 紧握；n. 控制}}{{Fear gripped the crowd as the storm approached.}}

{{hamper}}{/ˈhæmpər/}}{v. 妨碍；阻碍}}{{The bad weather hampered rescue efforts.}}

{{harass}}{/ˈhærəs/}}{v. 骚扰；烦扰}}{{The company was fined for harassing its employees.}}

{{hazard}}{/ˈhæzərd/}}{n. 危险；风险}}{{Smoking is a serious health hazard.}}

{{heritage}}{/ˈherɪtɪdʒ/}}{n. 遗产；传统}}{{The country is proud of its rich cultural heritage.}}

{{hinder}}{/ˈhɪndər/}}{v. 阻碍；妨碍}}{{Lack of funding hinders the progress of the research.}}

{{hypothesis}}{/haɪˈpɒθəsɪs/}}{n. 假设；假说}}{{The scientist tested the hypothesis through experiments.}}

{{ideology}}{/ˌaɪdiˈɒlədʒi/}}{n. 意识形态；思想体系}}{{Political ideology influences policy decisions.}}

{{illuminate}}{/ɪˈluːmɪneɪt/}}{v. 照亮；阐明}}{{The study illuminates the relationship between poverty and health.}}

{{immense}}{/ɪˈmens/}}{adj. 巨大的；无限的}}{{The universe is immensely vast and mysterious.}}

{{impair}}{/ɪmˈpeər/}}{v. 损害；削弱}}{{Excessive noise can impair hearing over time.}}

{{imperative}}{/ɪmˈperətɪv/}}{adj. 必要的；n. 命令}}{{It is imperative that we act quickly to address the crisis.}}

{{implicit}}{/ɪmˈplɪsɪt/}}{adj. 含蓄的；隐含的}}{{There was an implicit understanding between them.}}

{{impose}}{/ɪmˈpəʊz/}}{v. 施加；强制执行}}{{The authority imposed a curfew during the emergency.}}

{{impulse}}{/ˈɪmpʌls/}}{n. 冲动；脉冲}}{{She bought the dress on impulse without thinking twice.}}

{{inaugurate}}{/ɪˈnɔːɡjəreɪt/}}{v. 开创；为...举行就职典礼}}{{The new president was inaugurated in a grand ceremony.}}

{{incidence}}{/ˈɪnsɪdəns/}}{n. 发生率}}{{The incidence of heart disease has increased in recent years.}}

{{inclined}}{/ɪnˈklaɪnd/}}{adj. 倾向于...的}}{{She is inclined to agree with the proposal.}}

{{incorporate}}{/ɪnˈkɔːrpəreɪt/}}{v. 合并；包含}}{{The new design incorporates the latest technology.}}

{{incur}}{/ɪnˈkɜːr/}}{v. 招致；遭受}}{{The company incurred heavy losses during the recession.}}

{{indifferent}}{/ɪnˈdɪfərənt/}}{adj. 漠不关心的}}{{He seemed indifferent to the outcome of the negotiations.}}

{{indispensable}}{/ˌɪndɪˈspensəbl/}}{adj. 不可或缺的}}{{Clean water is indispensable for human survival.}}

{{induce}}{/ɪnˈdjuːs/}}{v. 引起；诱导}}{{Stress can induce a variety of health problems.}}

{{infer}}{/ɪnˈfɜːr/}}{v. 推断；推论}}{{From the data, we can infer that the trend will continue.}}

{{infrastructure}}{/ˈɪnfrəstrʌktʃər/}}{n. 基础设施}}{{The government invested heavily in transportation infrastructure.}}

{{inherent}}{/ɪnˈhɪərənt/}}{adj. 固有的；内在的}}{{There are inherent risks in any business venture.}}

{{inhibit}}{/ɪnˈhɪbɪt/}}{v. 抑制；阻碍}}{{Fear can inhibit people from taking action.}}

{{inject}}{/ɪnˈdʒekt/}}{v. 注射；注入}}{{The government injected资金 into the struggling economy.}}

{{innovative}}{/ˈɪnəveɪtɪv/}}{adj. 创新的；革新的}}{{The company is known for its innovative products.}}

{{integral}}{/ˈɪntɪɡrəl/}}{adj. 不可或缺的；完整的}}{{Teamwork is integral to the success of the project.}}

{{integrate}}{/ˈɪntɪɡreɪt/}}{v. 整合；融入}}{{The school integrates technology into its teaching methods.}}

{{integrity}}{/ɪnˈteɡrəti/}}{n. 正直；完整性}}{{He is a man of integrity who always keeps his promises.}}

{{intensify}}{/ɪnˈtensɪfaɪ/}}{v. 加剧；增强}}{{The competition in the market has intensified in recent years.}}
